# Recovery-mode init. Lands at the root of the recovery ramdisk, where init
# picks it up as /init.recovery.${ro.hardware}.rc — ro.hardware is mt6789,
# appended to the cmdline by the LK.
#
# Without this the recovery ramdisk has no USB gadget configuration at all, so
# `adb sideload` — the way this ROM is installed — never enumerates.
#
# Derived from stock revision 28's copy, with two removals:
#   * import /init.recovery.project.rc — no such file ships in revision 28.
#   * an `on boot` exec of /system/bin/mtk_plpath_utils, which builds the
#     legacy /dev/block/platform/... symlink tree. This tree does not install
#     that binary into the recovery ramdisk, and everything here addresses
#     partitions through /dev/block/by-name, which ueventd creates.

on init
    setprop sys.usb.configfs 1
    setprop sys.usb.controller "musb-hdrc"
    setprop sys.usb.ffs.aio_compat 0

on fs && property:ro.debuggable=0
    # Tell the charger whether USB is a CDP or an SDP port. Without this the
    # port is treated as charging-only and waits for USB activation that never
    # comes.
    write /sys/class/udc/musb-hdrc/device/cmode 2
    start adbd
